{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings","id":789178,"title":"Exigence and Dragon Kings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-19T02:59:55-08:00","id":789178,"title":"Exigence and Dragon Kings","content":"So... i am going to avoid spelling hazards by referring to the... err... O..ochilekay? You know what I mean. I will call them Exigents, in the theory of this post. So. We all know the idea of Exigence is old. Well, what if it predated humanity? Before true exaltation was fashioned and mastered by a titan, the dragon kings knew of such a force, passed from the Sun to other gods, allowing some dragon kings to become heroes of their own kind.. Well... what if in 3e, it isnt just shoddy knockoffs of CoD's Claimed, but rather.. the Exigence? What if Exigence is less.... cheap, knock off, easily tweaked Exaltation. What if its the original? What if the Dragon King's Ochilike (again, i am butcherihg spelling) were the protoexalted, and Autocthon spent a long time perfecting the idea of gods becoming men? Is it possible the dragon kings cannot exalt, but can become exigents? Is it possible exigents predated humanity, and the human ability to handle the divine fire? Is it possible the decline of dragon king society is because many gods with stable exigencies have moved them to monkey rather than reptile? Is the decline of dragon king society based on how Exigency is now spent on men, and not them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T03:29:35-08:00","id":789182,"title":"","content":"It's unlikely. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Exigence is less.... cheap, knock off, easily tweaked Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div> This part is probably right on the money, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T03:51:02-08:00","id":789189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings#post789178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... i am going to avoid spelling hazards by referring to the... err... O..ochilekay? You know what I mean. I will call them Exigents, in the theory of this post. So. We all know the idea of Exigence is old. Well, what if it predated humanity? Before true exaltation was fashioned and mastered by a titan, the dragon kings knew of such a force, passed from the Sun to other gods, allowing some dragon kings to become heroes of their own kind.. Well... what if in 3e, it isnt just shoddy knockoffs of CoD's Claimed,</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, i think those ones are the Liminals, not the Exigents. Ah, sorry, Claimed, not Created. Anyway, pretty loose connection through the &quot;anything goes&quot; tie to spirits, i guess...<br /> <br /> About the Dragon King's Olchilike as an actual sort of exalt pre-human origin, i think it has been considerably hinted, if not outright said, the book on the Niobrarian's resistance against early First Age Deliberative will have some of that in it. Anyway, wait and see i guess.<br /> <br /> Edit: No, wait, <b>Olchilik\u00e9</b> are like some sort of shoddy knockoffs of CoD's Claimed, not Exigents, that's what you actually meant, no?<br /> Makes much more sense, though i think they actually came first, so technically the Claimed might be the actual knockoffs...<br /> <br /> Anyways, really shouldn't go reading - and answering stuff barely 10 minutes after getting out of bed. Sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-19-2015, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T04:07:11-08:00","id":789194,"title":"","content":"The problem with this theory, of course, is that Exigence <i>is</i> Exaltation, while the <i>olchilik\u00e9</i> were just cases of willing possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 12-19-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T04:17:19-08:00","id":789197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings?p=789194#post789194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this theory, of course, is that Exigence <i>is</i> Exaltation, while the <i>olchilik\u00e9</i> were just cases of willing possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, the book themselves point to High Holy Speech using the same word for both states - &quot;infused/imbued with the majesty/might of the gods&quot;, so to speak. A connection to Exigence from the point the concept is introduced to the setting is not out of the bag, far from it, i guess. Not to mention that considering that some mid- to high-tier gods can make avatars/duplicates of themselves, the line between being infused with a fragment of the god's essence and symbiotic possession can become even more razor-thin and blurry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-18-2026, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T05:05:41-08:00","id":789207,"title":"","content":"I don't like the idea that Ochilike were Exigents, because they're quite distinctive things - ochilike is a shamanic merging with a god, which Exigency doesn't seem to be (as much as it can be whatever!). <br /> <br /> Although on a similar note, I like that there might have been some competition between Olichike and Exigency though, that could've led to the decline of the former and the decline of the Dragon King civilization.<br /> <br /> Together with a change in the deities themselves from a rawer and more many bodied / multi-local form that could take part in the ochilike ritual to one which was singular, separate and met the bureaucratic ideal, and the ideal of the gods being separate from man, and would prefer Exigence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:52:59-08:00","id":789260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings?p=789207#post789207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the idea that Ochilike were Exigents, because they're quite distinctive things - ochilike is a shamanic merging with a god, which Exigency doesn't seem to be (as much as it can be whatever!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as discussed in another topic, Exigence covers a wide range of possibilities - not all of them literal Exigence gifted by the UCS - that may include weird twists and varieties in the usual logic of how exalts work, so it might be an option.<br /> <br /> The Niobraran's brand of Chosen - that while not Exigents per se might be devised using the guidelines for them, from what has been said so far - whole point seem to be that they break with the &quot;only human&quot; criterium of Exaltation, for example. Overall it's a matter of wait and see, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-18-2026, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T08:51:17-08:00","id":789269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings?p=789260#post789260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Niobraran's brand of Chosen - that while not Exigents per se might make be devised using the guidelines for them, from wha has been said so far - whole point seem to be that they break with the &quot;only human&quot; criterium of Exaltation, for example. Overall it's a matter of wait and see, i guess.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's been mentioned that the Niobaran League included pelagothropes which as human mutants are capable of Exaltation. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:08:23-08:00","id":789289,"title":"","content":"Olchilik\u00e9 are cool enough that I'd just want to bring them back as they were, instead of trying to shove them into a different box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:28:56-08:00","id":789302,"title":"","content":"Maybe Dragon Kings will have a power comparable to Divine Mantle to facilitate them becoming Olchilik\u00e9, rather than relying on a very specific (and forbidden) spirit Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T15:55:31-08:00","id":789454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings?p=789269#post789269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's been mentioned that the Niobaran League included pelagothropes which as human mutants are capable of Exaltation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes for an interesting workaround indeed - and setting-wise would seem to establish the probable existence of pretty ancient tribes or nations of mutated humans existing under the seas long before the Primordial War, not unlike some of the Underbroods in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/789178-exigence-and-dragon-kings?p=789302#post789302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Dragon Kings will have a power comparable to Divine Mantle to facilitate them becoming Olchilik\u00e9, rather than relying on a very specific (and forbidden) spirit Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The charm per se is far from forbidden, afaik - it's simply a variant of possession that is seem as mostly outdated and of limited use without many cultures with similar esoteric beliefs around in Creation. A more specialized form of possession and one of very little benefit to the spirit per se in relation to the basic one, more so with no society of people actively seeking out to serve as their vessels.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it ain't something like a Forbidden Path or such, far from it in fact and it might be possible that some cultures somewhat influenced by Dragon King mysticism - like the barbarian and mutant tribes around Rathess, or maybe, just maybe, some esoteric fraternities like Shining Flower's cult or some conservative and knowledgeable savants in the Varang City-States, or whatever a ST comes up with - still have practices connected to Olchilike. In fact it might count as a way to get around caste and astrologic restrictions in their culture (&quot;it wasn't me, it was the will of the gods acting through my hand&quot;) beside manipulating foreigners.<br /> <br /> The Olchilik\u00e9 are a most interesting concept with lots of possibility, but i think it might benefit even more of some retooling in both mechanics and fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-19-2015, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}